{
  "lane": "rust",
  "status_key": "__rust_status__",
  "origin": "rust",
  "reference": "rust-tools.md",
  "finding_const": {
    "fix_recipe": null
  },
  "_note": "Every invocation names the target explicitly (`--file` / `--manifest-path`): a bare `cargo audit` runs in the RUNNER's cwd, so the lane used to scan whatever tree it was invoked from. CARGO_TARGET_DIR points at the scratch dir because cargo-geiger compiles the crate and would otherwise fill `target/` inside the caller's project. Field maps follow the shapes cargo-audit 0.22 / cargo-deny 0.19 / cargo-geiger 0.13 actually emit (captured in tests/fixtures/raw-tool-output/rust/), not the hand-authored ones the lane carried before 2026-09-02, which matched nothing.",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "cargo-audit",
      "probe": "cargo-audit",
      "applicable_glob": "Cargo.lock",
      "inapplicable_reason": "no-lockfile",
      "invoke": [
        "cargo",
        "audit",
        "--json",
        "--file",
        "{target}/Cargo.lock"
      ],
      "output": "stdout",
      "findings_path": "vulnerabilities.list",
      "const": {
        "confidence": "high",
        "file": "Cargo.lock",
        "line": 0
      },
      "map": {
        "id": {
          "from": "advisory.aliases.0",
          "fallback": {
            "from": "advisory.id"
          }
        },
        "severity": {
          "from": "advisory.cvss",
          "cvss_band": true,
          "default": "MEDIUM"
        },
        "cwe": {
          "from": "advisory.cwe.0",
          "default": "CWE-1104"
        },
        "title": "advisory.title",
        "evidence": {
          "from": "advisory.description",
          "truncate": 300,
          "default": ""
        },
        "reference_url": {
          "concat": [
            "https://rustsec.org/advisories/",
            {
              "from": "advisory.id"
            },
            ".html"
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "fix_recipe": {
          "concat": [
            "Upgrade ",
            {
              "from": "package.name"
            },
            " to ",
            {
              "from": "versions.patched.0"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "_note": "`advisory.cvss` is a vector string, not a score, so cvss_band falls to MEDIUM; the cve-enricher re-scores by CVE id downstream. cargo-audit ships no CWE; CWE-1104 is the documented fallback (rust-runner.md)."
    },
    {
      "name": "cargo-deny",
      "probe": "cargo-deny",
      "applicable_glob": "Cargo.toml",
      "inapplicable_reason": "no-manifest",
      "invoke": [
        "cargo",
        "deny",
        "--manifest-path",
        "{target}/Cargo.toml",
        "--format",
        "json",
        "check"
      ],
      "env": {
        "CARGO_TARGET_DIR": "{tmp}/target"
      },
      "output": "stderr",
      "input_format": "jsonl",
      "filter": [
        {
          "field": "type",
          "equals": "diagnostic"
        },
        {
          "field": "fields.code",
          "not_in": [
            "accepted",
            "rejected",
            "unlicensed",
            "no-license-field",
            "license-not-encountered",
            "license-exception-not-encountered",
            "missing-clarification-file",
            "deprecated",
            "unused-license-exception",
            "unused-licenses-allowed",
            "allowed",
            "allowed-source",
            "allowed-by-organization",
            "allowed-by-wrapper",
            "skipped",
            "skipped-by-root",
            "advisory-ignored",
            "advisory-not-detected",
            "yanked-ignored",
            "yanked-not-detected",
            "checksum-match",
            "unmatched-source",
            "unmatched-organization",
            "unmatched-bypass",
            "unmatched-glob",
            "unmatched-path-bypass",
            "unmatched-root",
            "unmatched-skip",
            "unmatched-skip-root",
            "unmatched-wrapper",
            "unnecessary-skip",
            "unused-wrapper",
            "unused-workspace-dependency",
            "path-bypassed",
            "path-bypassed-by-glob",
            "index-cache-load-failure",
            "index-failure",
            "unknown-advisory",
            "empty-license-field",
            "gather-failure",
            "parse-error",
            "skipped-private-workspace-crate"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "const": {
        "confidence": "medium",
        "reference_url": null,
        "file": "Cargo.lock"
      },
      "map": {
        "id": "fields.code",
        "severity": {
          "from": "fields.severity",
          "map": {
            "error": "HIGH",
            "warning": "MEDIUM",
            "note": "LOW",
            "help": "LOW"
          },
          "default": "MEDIUM"
        },
        "cwe": {
          "from": "fields.code",
          "lookup": {
            "vulnerability": "CWE-1395",
            "unsound": "CWE-1395",
            "unmaintained": "CWE-1104",
            "yanked": "CWE-1104",
            "wildcard": "CWE-1104",
            "source-not-allowed": "CWE-494",
            "git-source-underspecified": "CWE-494",
            "checksum-mismatch": "CWE-494",
            "detected-executable": "CWE-506",
            "detected-executable-script": "CWE-506",
            "build-script-not-allowed": "CWE-829"
          },
          "default": null
        },
        "title": "fields.message",
        "evidence": {
          "from": "fields.labels.0.span",
          "default": ""
        },
        "line": {
          "from": "fields.labels.0.line",
          "default": 0
        }
      },
      "_note": "Diagnostics go to STDERR (stdout stays empty) and nest under `fields` and carry `type: diagnostic|log|summary`; codes are words (`vulnerability`, `unmaintained`, `source-not-allowed`), not the A/B/S numbers the reference once described. The exclusion list drops licence and config-lint families so a target without deny.toml does not drown in `rejected: license is not explicitly allowed`; any code cargo-deny adds later passes through."
    },
    {
      "name": "cargo-geiger",
      "probe": "cargo-geiger",
      "applicable_glob": "Cargo.toml",
      "inapplicable_reason": "no-manifest",
      "invoke": [
        "cargo",
        "geiger",
        "--manifest-path",
        "{target}/Cargo.toml",
        "--output-format",
        "Json"
      ],
      "env": {
        "CARGO_TARGET_DIR": "{tmp}/target"
      },
      "output": "stdout",
      "findings_path": "packages",
      "filter": {
        "field": "unsafety.used.exprs.unsafe_",
        "gt": 0
      },
      "const": {
        "confidence": "low",
        "severity": "INFO",
        "cwe": null,
        "line": 0,
        "reference_url": null
      },
      "map": {
        "id": {
          "concat": [
            {
              "from": "package.id.name"
            },
            "@",
            {
              "from": "package.id.version"
            }
          ]
        },
        "title": {
          "concat": [
            "Unsafe code in ",
            {
              "from": "package.id.name"
            }
          ]
        },
        "file": "package.id.name",
        "evidence": {
          "concat": [
            {
              "from": "package.id.name"
            },
            "@",
            {
              "from": "package.id.version"
            },
            ": unsafe code used — functions=",
            {
              "from": "unsafety.used.functions.unsafe_"
            },
            ", exprs=",
            {
              "from": "unsafety.used.exprs.unsafe_"
            },
            ", methods=",
            {
              "from": "unsafety.used.methods.unsafe_"
            },
            ", impls=",
            {
              "from": "unsafety.used.item_impls.unsafe_"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "_note": "Only packages whose USED unsafe expression count is non-zero become findings; the rest of the tree is listed by the tool but is not a signal. INFO is a ceiling (rust-runner.md hard rule 7)."
    }
  ]
}
